<section class="sj-section" id="what-57">
  <div class="sj-wrap">
    <h2>What “{{ C.counts.inherited }}” means</h2>
    <p>The map’s core is {{ C.counts.inherited }} <b>descriptions of God</b> drawn from the Apostles’, Nicene, and Athanasian Creeds, the Fourth Lateran Council, the Augsburg Confession, the Thirty-Nine Articles, the Westminster Confession, and other historic formularies: God is living, true, Father, almighty, merciful, invisible, without body, unchangeable, and so on. Each description was compared with authoritative Latter-day Saint teaching and placed in one of three categories.</p>
    <p>These are descriptions of God, not a list of every Christian doctrine. The map does not count teachings about the Church, sacraments, salvation, or the end of the world, and it does not by itself decide the question of the Trinity—which has its own panel below. {{ C.counts.additions }} additional Restoration teachings, mostly about who human beings are and what they may become, are counted separately because they do not appear in the creeds at all.</p>
    {{ twoBars(C.counts) }}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sj-section" id="categories">
  <div class="sj-wrap">
    <h2>The four categories, in plain words</h2>
    <table class="sj-cattable">
      <thead><tr><th>On the map</th><th>What it means</th><th>The sentence you can say</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>{{ chip("A", C.code_labels, "lg") }}</td><td>Both traditions affirm this of God in the same sense.</td><td><em>{{ C.four_clause.A }}</em></td></tr>
        <tr><td>{{ chip("Q", C.code_labels, "lg") }}</td><td>Both use the word and share the concern, but the picture behind it differs—the <em>how</em> or the <em>what kind</em>.</td><td><em>{{ C.four_clause.Q }}</em></td></tr>
        <tr><td>{{ chip("D", C.code_labels, "lg") }}</td><td>At the level the creeds intend, the two teachings cannot both be true.</td><td><em>{{ C.four_clause.D }}</em></td></tr>
        <tr><td>{{ chip("ADDITION", C.code_labels, "lg") }}</td><td>A teaching the creeds and confessions studied do not contain as a positive doctrine.</td><td><em>{{ C.four_clause.ADDITION }}</em></td></tr>
