<section class="sj-section" id="numbers">
  <div class="sj-wrap">
    <h2>How to read the numbers</h2>
    <p>Every statistic on this site shows three things: the <b>count</b>, the <b>percentage</b>, and, where the research supports one, the <b>range</b> it moves within when the coding is weighted for how central a doctrine is. All three carry a <em>provisional</em> mark. For example:</p>
    {{ stat(C.stats.shared_floor_A_plus_Q, "inherited descriptions share a conceptual floor (Shared + Shared, differently understood)") }}
    <div class="sj-grid" style="margin-top:.6rem">
      <div>{{ stat(C.stats.strict_A, "affirmed in the same sense") }}</div>
      <div>{{ stat(C.stats.direct_D, "directly different") }}</div>
    </div>
    <p>The coding was done inside this project and has not yet been independently replicated by outside scholars. The numbers describe this bounded comparison; they do not measure “Christianity,” and they never rank one denomination as closer or farther than another. The site will not show you a denomination ranking, because the evidence is not complete enough to support one honestly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

