    <p class="sj-mute">On the left, the creedal Shield of the Trinity: the Father is God, the Son is God, the Holy Spirit is God; the Father is not the Son, the Son is not the Spirit, the Spirit is not the Father. On the right, the Latter-day Saint Godhead: the Father, the Son, and the Holy Ghost are each divine and together are one Godhead; each is a separate being; the Father presides, and prayer is offered to the Father in the name of the Son. The one counted description that touches this structure—“neither confounding the persons nor dividing the substance”—is coded <em>shared, but differently understood</em> (<a href="/seeking-jesus/map/#RNR-H56">RNR-H56</a>).</p>
