<section class="sj-section" id="clarifications">
  <div class="sj-wrap">
    <h2>About the Clarifications explorer</h2>
    <p>Some misunderstandings are not about any single description of God. They come from a slogan, a shared word, or a difference in how a tradition governs itself. The Clarifications explorer holds short cases that untangle those—the first two are a Baptist case and a Latter-day Saint case on the same fault line, faith and works. These cases reach beyond the {{ C.counts.inherited }} descriptions, they are never counted, and a case appears automatically only once per view and only when it is relevant to what you are reading.</p>
    <div class="sj-grid">
      {% for cs in C.clarifications.cases %}
      <details class="sj-card">
        <summary>{{ cs.title }} <span class="sj-mute">({{ cs.tradition }})</span></summary>
        <p><b>{{ cs.question }}</b></p>
        <p>{{ cs.distinction }}</p>
        <p>{{ cs.resolution }}</p>
        <p class="sj-caution"><b>What this case does not prove.</b> {{ cs.does_not_prove }}</p>
        <p class="sj-sources">Sources: {% for src in cs.sources %}<a href="{{ src.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ src.document }}{% if src.locator %}, {{ src.locator }}{% endif %}</a>{% if not loop.last %} &middot; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
      </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sj-section" id="how-made">
  <div class="sj-wrap">
    <h2>How this map was made</h2>
    <div class="sj-provenance">
      <p>This study was prepared by Aaron J. Powner for Words of Plainness Ministry. Historic descriptions of God were drawn from official creeds, councils, confessions, and catechisms, and every citation links to the text on the publishing tradition’s own site; every quoted phrase is checked against that text each time the site is built. Latter-day Saint comparators are drawn from canonized scripture, official Church publications, and General Conference addresses, with the source level shown on each card.</p>
      <p>The classification of each description was carried out within this project with the assistance of an AI system, then reviewed and ratified line by line by the author. The results are internally consistent but have not yet been independently replicated by outside scholars, and they are labeled <em>provisional</em> wherever they appear. A denomination-by-denomination view exists in the research files but is withheld from this site until its evidence is complete enough to display fairly.</p>
      <p class="sj-meta">Data version {{ C.version }} &middot; {{ C.counts.inherited }} inherited descriptions, {{ C.counts.additions }} Restoration additions &middot; pipeline run {{ C.run_at }} &middot; corrections are welcome through the <a href="/connect/">connect page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

